            "review_text": "maryyeo\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam4531 contributions\n1\nHarry Potter cafe. Good for families.\nAug 2018 • Family\nA lovely addition to the stretch of restaurants along the Crescent Lake.\n\nWe liked their Harry Potter deco (obviously the huge train mural, the wizard's uniform, the caged white owl and the 9 and 3/4 platform all point to the story!), the high ceilings and glass windows letting plenty of natural light in, their wide Scandinavian wooden tables both in and outdoor, and even their cosy and cushioned booth seats. \n\nWe also liked that they serve good quality food - the simplest item on our dish - the bread (choose from carrot, whole grain or wheat) - tasted so moist, fresh and it was served hot. The beef was tender and flavorful. The bacons were crisped to the right texture.\n\nWhat we liked the most, was that they cater to families. They're open bright and early at 6am, so we could catch a wonderful breakfast with the kids and watch the lake glisten in the morning sun. They do their pancakes well too - all fluffy, served with maple syrup, cream, fruits and jam all in cute little ramekins on the side. On their two hanging LED TVs, the non-stop video on creative foods on Youtube was surprisingly fascinating and addictive to watch for both adults and kids. They even provided a small double swing and two rocking horses outside, not too fanciful, but good enough to satisfy the toddlers a little while. Oh, and their servers are professionally courteous, friendly, and speak English.\n\nTheir prices may be above average for this city, but still affordable. And for this quality and atmosphere, it's still much cheaper compared to Singapore or Hong Kong.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten August 15, 2018",
