            "review_text": "needlehill\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam454 contributions\n1\nGood but sooo expensive...\nFeb 2018 • Solo\nMy only experience at Kingscross was a good one.\nI specially liked the salad with barramundi. My small pizza was tasty also.\nFor those who know it, the area is probably the most pleasant in Saigon (with the lake called Hồ bán nguyệt, meaning half-circle lake).\nThe only problem is the prices. Very, very high. Almost fine dining prices for food that isn't fine dining, although it's good.\nI had relatively affordable dishes in order not to get a ridiculous final bill. But if you go for their main courses, ouch!\nFor people who never eat good food at home, I can understand. Otherwise...\nThere seem to be a set lunch, so I'm eager to try it to have the chance to experience more dishes and have a full meal.\nBut anyway, price is a big issue, and the restaurant will never be full because of that. Just look at others around... (Tokyo Deli, Hoang Yen for ex)\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten May 14, 2018",
